        intro: "Acute soft-tissue injuries — sprains, strains, muscle tears within the first 42 days — require two sequential repair signals: immediate vascular ingrowth and NO-mediated inflammation modulation (BPC-157), followed by accelerated cell migration and anti-fibrotic proliferative repair (TB-500). This 2-peptide stack addresses the two primary failure modes in acute healing: insufficient early angiogenesis and delayed proliferative phase transition. For chronic tendinopathy, post-surgical rehabilitation, or injuries beyond 6–8 weeks, see the dedicated injury-recovery page.",
